ough the roof the  toxicity over time obviously falls in in  the in the in the city because they're  these took trucks are no longer pumping  out the emissions right there is  absolutely no  season and I don't think from my  perspective any of us should have a  problem with the fact that this  hopefully one day will be a  multi-billion dollar company we could  also significantly significantly impact  pollution rates and health amongst the  poorest of the poor urban dwellers  tuk-tuk drivers in a range of countries  that to me is it is a pure impact  investment win-win where you've got a  sort of uber profit motive if you will  and a lot of money eventually being made  with an extraordinary private sector  resolution to a problem which certainly  the public sector in the government  hasn't touched or being able to do  anything about but having said that not  every business has such a perfect  symbiosis if you will between the social  and the and the and the profit side or  the financial side so your point is also  well taken that's what makes it so  complicated
 

